{"sha":"8dd5d6a7e12689d047ca309e0d367c6868f388e9","node_id":"C_kwDOOeTgGNoAKDhkZDVkNmE3ZTEyNjg5ZDA0N2NhMzA5ZTBkMzY3YzY4NjhmMzg4ZTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"ilaigold","email":"117302862+ilaigold@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-10-07T08:16:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-10-07T08:16:51Z"},"message":"auth: check token expiry before required scopes (#1350)\n\nWhile reading `RequireBearerToken` I noticed that `verify` checks\nrequired scopes before expiry. A token that's expired and also missing a\nscope gets `403 insufficient scope` instead of `401 token expired`, and\na token with no expiration gets the same 403 when\n`AllowMissingExpiration` is false. Repro is in #1349.\n\nAn expired token is `invalid_token` (RFC 6750 §3.1), so the client\nshould be told to get a new token, not to ask for more scopes. I moved\nthe expiry check, including the missing-expiration case, above the scope\nloop. No API change.\n\nThis touches the same lines in `verify` and `TestVerify` as #1135. If\nthat one lands first I'll rebase on it.\n\nTested with go1.27.1 on darwin/arm64:\n\n- The two new `TestVerify` cases (\"expired and missing scope\", \"no\nexpiration and missing scope\") fail on main with `got (\"insufficient\nscope\", 403)` and pass with the fix.\n- `gofmt -l auth` and `go vet ./...` are clean, and `go test -count=1\n./...` passes.\n- The repro from the issue now prints `401 token expired`.\n\nFixes #1349\n\n_AI assistance: I used Claude Code to help write this fix and the\ntests._\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dabcc7284baaffc5d216f0b84d6df045049085ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/git/trees/dabcc7284baaffc5d216f0b84d6df045049085ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/git/commits/8dd5d6a7e12689d047ca309e0d367c6868f388e9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxf/zCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABHsQAIdgkQsA4K/GneMmR980aaHQ\nRQQv1FlTrszPdwuMj83cf5t0J445X5QaGBkvLahMxjUlglvTRUPffDarIIve4pT9\nsSC+U1IfwJjEx281xY7RXDMFcm++vqdeomnjj+NeTeFGxKg9KE3r/IxZrN6aPwhF\nbEKq7VDlQO80iH2uzkXI31r6oQn/xt9BjTEj11WtyFS0NBh5NZNsrKTABYBD0wk4\noDwcRZC0jr+4lgDYCdOQEaqh/BuhEvBlYEgfTmM17JIIvL7Yy1VYFwLJjwBwFiEf\n6sDmm5vLAM1E+Dxu1F+LwHj0IdqUPfQpf/VDNp0W5L+ncKtPOLMoWWxHWQrD9eEn\nEI844lGanTkUX5eFX9rRf8Re7EcDibKqypNI2bytTwDKp59/SFT64fVH7Zclh3U1\nRPSSGP2gaxzTjJ9R2q7MJvbFnyOmDAFzGcFppiI1lwa8DId6auo4kPxQmcxw5cgy\n5peFBZ7DdTxwhT1msMEen4KAxpWeIvUrMlArMzf9aOs7GnoyoSnwsSkhCaW4/2Ph\n/MVGhdZPbb2L5PgGS3eey8slRIie7a5BpOM7A12VFdS4XhNh58CznHb6s48sDyxY\nNT3X9lKGMIrMG5tYA1D/N0dQXJd+7E6UFul5sq5tXeMqAP5Hz9XP84KIZNUo8ZDF\nxkBoB4sNHJE6qVgOeC5z\n=IdYo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree dabcc7284baaffc5d216f0b84d6df045049085ad\nparent 6737e73d2da2251423eabc3c2e1fb77f25186360\nauthor ilaigold <117302862+ilaigold@users.noreply.github.com> 1791361011 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791361011 +0200\n\nauth: check token expiry before required scopes (#1350)\n\nWhile reading `RequireBearerToken` I noticed that `verify` checks\nrequired scopes before expiry. A token that's expired and also missing a\nscope gets `403 insufficient scope` instead of `401 token expired`, and\na token with no expiration gets the same 403 when\n`AllowMissingExpiration` is false. Repro is in #1349.\n\nAn expired token is `invalid_token` (RFC 6750 §3.1), so the client\nshould be told to get a new token, not to ask for more scopes. I moved\nthe expiry check, including the missing-expiration case, above the scope\nloop. No API change.\n\nThis touches the same lines in `verify` and `TestVerify` as #1135. If\nthat one lands first I'll rebase on it.\n\nTested with go1.27.1 on darwin/arm64:\n\n- The two new `TestVerify` cases (\"expired and missing scope\", \"no\nexpiration and missing scope\") fail on main with `got (\"insufficient\nscope\", 403)` and pass with the fix.\n- `gofmt -l auth` and `go vet ./...` are clean, and `go test -count=1\n./...` passes.\n- The repro from the issue now prints `401 token expired`.\n\nFixes #1349\n\n_AI assistance: I used Claude Code to help write this fix and the\ntests._\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-10-07T08:16:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/commits/8dd5d6a7e12689d047ca309e0d367c6868f388e9","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/commit/8dd5d6a7e12689d047ca309e0d367c6868f388e9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/commits/8dd5d6a7e12689d047ca309e0d367c6868f388e9/comments","author":{"login":"ilaigold","id":117302862,"node_id":"U_kgDOBv3mTg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/117302862?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilaigold","html_url":"https://github.com/ilaigold","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilaigold/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilaigold/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilaigold/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilaigold/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilaigold/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilaigold/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilaigold/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilaigold/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilaigold/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6737e73d2da2251423eabc3c2e1fb77f25186360","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/commits/6737e73d2da2251423eabc3c2e1fb77f25186360","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/commit/6737e73d2da2251423eabc3c2e1fb77f25186360"}],"stats":{"total":29,"additions":19,"deletions":10},"files":[{"sha":"7eb20b129ec7b836d5eec6dc003c8fdcef9089d9","filename":"auth/auth.go","status":"modified","additions":11,"deletions":10,"changes":21,"blob_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/blob/8dd5d6a7e12689d047ca309e0d367c6868f388e9/auth%2Fauth.go","raw_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/raw/8dd5d6a7e12689d047ca309e0d367c6868f388e9/auth%2Fauth.go","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/contents/auth%2Fauth.go?ref=8dd5d6a7e12689d047ca309e0d367c6868f388e9","patch":"@@ -147,29 +147,30 @@ func verify(req *http.Request, verifier TokenVerifier, opts *RequireBearerTokenO\n \t\treturn nil, \"token validation failed\", http.StatusInternalServerError\n \t}\n \n-\t// Check scopes. All must be present.\n-\tif opts != nil {\n-\t\t// Note: quadratic, but N is small.\n-\t\tfor _, s := range opts.Scopes {\n-\t\t\tif !slices.Contains(tokenInfo.Scopes, s) {\n-\t\t\t\treturn nil, \"insufficient scope\", http.StatusForbidden\n-\t\t\t}\n-\t\t}\n-\t}\n-\n \tif opts == nil {\n \t\topts = &RequireBearerTokenOptions{}\n \t}\n \t// Check expiration, with optional clock-skew tolerance. Skew only applies\n \t// when an expiration is present; a missing expiration is governed solely by\n \t// AllowMissingExpiration.\n+\t// This runs before the scope check so that an expired token is rejected\n+\t// as invalid (401), prompting the client to get a new token, rather than\n+\t// as lacking scope (403), prompting it to ask for more scopes.\n \tif tokenInfo.Expiration.IsZero() {\n \t\tif !opts.AllowMissingExpiration {\n \t\t\treturn nil, \"token missing expiration\", http.StatusUnauthorized\n \t\t}\n \t} else if tokenInfo.Expiration.Add(opts.ClockSkew).Before(time.Now()) {\n \t\treturn nil, \"token expired\", http.StatusUnauthorized\n \t}\n+\n+\t// Check scopes. All must be present.\n+\t// Note: quadratic, but N is small.\n+\tfor _, s := range opts.Scopes {\n+\t\tif !slices.Contains(tokenInfo.Scopes, s) {\n+\t\t\treturn nil, \"insufficient scope\", http.StatusForbidden\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n \treturn tokenInfo, \"\", 0\n }\n "},{"sha":"5fa923f604f3524b821c0dfd0539649b2b0f4473","filename":"auth/auth_test.go","status":"modified","additions":8,"deletions":0,"changes":8,"blob_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/blob/8dd5d6a7e12689d047ca309e0d367c6868f388e9/auth%2Fauth_test.go","raw_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/raw/8dd5d6a7e12689d047ca309e0d367c6868f388e9/auth%2Fauth_test.go","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/contents/auth%2Fauth_test.go?ref=8dd5d6a7e12689d047ca309e0d367c6868f388e9","patch":"@@ -75,6 +75,14 @@ func TestVerify(t *testing.T) {\n \t\t\t\"missing scope\", &RequireBearerTokenOptions{Scopes: []string{\"s1\"}}, \"Bearer valid\",\n \t\t\t\"insufficient scope\", 403,\n \t\t},\n+\t\t{\n+\t\t\t\"expired and missing scope\", &RequireBearerTokenOptions{Scopes: []string{\"s1\"}}, \"Bearer expired\",\n+\t\t\t\"token expired\", 401,\n+\t\t},\n+\t\t{\n+\t\t\t\"no expiration and missing scope\", &RequireBearerTokenOptions{Scopes: []string{\"s1\"}}, \"Bearer noexp\",\n+\t\t\t\"token missing expiration\", 401,\n+\t\t},\n \t} {\n \t\tt.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n \t\t\t_, gotMsg, gotCode := verify(&http.Request{"}]}